Retrieve the list of contacts and their associated domains and roles.
You can filter the list by domain name.

USAGE:
  scw domain contact list [arg=value ...]

ARGS:
  [domain]            Filter contacts by domain name.
  [project-id]        Filter contacts by project ID.
  [role]              Filter contacts by role (owner, administrative, technical). (unknown_role | owner | administrative | technical)
  [email-status]      Filter contacts by email validation status. (email_status_unknown | validated | not_validated | invalid_email)
  [order-by]          Sort order of the returned contacts (created_at_asc | created_at_desc | email_asc | email_desc)
  [status]            Filter by contact status (status_unknown | active | pending)
  [legal-form]        Filter by legal form (legal_form_unknown | individual | corporate | association | other)
  [email]             Filter by email address
  [search]            Fuzzy search in firstname, lastname, email, and company_name
  [organization-id]   Filter contacts by organization ID.

FLAGS:
  -h, --help                help for list
      --list-sub-commands   List all subcommands

GLOBAL FLAGS:
  -B, --beta             Enable beta mode
  -c, --config string    The path to the config file
  -D, --debug            Enable debug mode
  -H, --no-headers       Skip headers in human output
  -o, --output string    Output format: json or human, see 'scw help output' for more info (default "human")
  -p, --profile string   The config profile to use
